error[LIMIT009]: `<raise>` event name `exxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 an event name may have
 --> tests/ui/limit009-names-over-name-bound.scx:4:21
  |
4 |       <raise event="exxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx...
  |                     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^ 1,025 bytes
  |
  = note: every build bounds an event name to 1,024 bytes of UTF-8, so this `<raise>` could never run as written; SCXML 1.0 sets no length, and this is the implementation's bound (spec errata L.6)
  = help: shorten the `event` value to at most 1,024 bytes
  = spec: SCXML 1.0 §4.2 <raise>

error[LIMIT009]: `<invoke>` ID `ixxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxxx…` is 1,013 bytes, so the `done.invoke.` event it raises is 1,025 bytes, more than the 1,024 an event name may have
